  "title": "Vertex conservation laws need not block hardness: conserved flows with a non-negative Fourier dual",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "When a gadget vertex reads the bracket of an edge's own leaves, its equations form a flow conserved at every vertex, and Fourier duality turns the count into a spin system on vertex states and potentials. If the flow vanishes off the diagonal and is bilinear on it, the weights are non-negative and the Brunnian rank witness gives #P-hardness, deciding 8 more census algebras.",
